<h2><strong>Important Factors to Check Before Purchasing</strong></h2>
<p>Selecting a cylinder based only on its product category can lead to installation problems. Before placing an order, review the following points.</p>
<p><strong>Bore diameter:</strong> Check the force required to move the load at the available operating pressure.</p>
<p><strong>Stroke length:</strong> Match the piston travel to the machine's actual movement requirements.</p>
<p><strong>Mounting arrangement:</strong> Verify mounting dimensions and available installation clearance.</p>
<p><strong>Piston rod specifications:</strong> Check rod diameter, thread and connection requirements.</p>
<p><strong>Air supply:</strong> Confirm that the compressor, directional control valve and tubing can support the required operation.</p>
<p><strong>Sensor compatibility:</strong> If the machine uses reed switches or other position sensors, verify the magnetic piston and sensor arrangement.</p>
<p><strong>Operating environment:</strong> Consider dust, moisture, temperature and operating frequency when selecting the cylinder and related accessories.</p>
<p>A complete specification check helps engineers select a cylinder that fits both the mechanical arrangement and the pneumatic system.</p>
